    {
      "id": "s2-intro",
      "type": "intro",
      "label": null,
      "title": "BEN — Just Like a Dream",
      "content": "Comparisons. \"Like a dream.\" \"Like a star.\"\n\nThis is a quiet, aching song about a love the singer can't tell was ever real. BEN spends the whole track circling one question: did I imagine how good that felt, or did you feel it too? He's caught between two people he's willing to accept — the one who loved him and the one who was only ever a dream — and he can't get either version to hold still.\n\nIn this lesson, you'll learn the grammar pattern **-처럼**, which means \"like, as.\" We'll see how BEN uses it in \"Just Like a Dream.\"",
      "musicPlaying": true
    },
    {
      "id": "s3-intro",
      "type": "intro",
      "label": null,
      "title": "이번에 배울 것",
      "content": "이번 레슨에서 배울 단어:\n- **별** — star\n- **꽃** — flower\n- **꿈처럼** — like a dream\n- **별처럼 빛나다** — to shine like a star\n\n레슨이 끝나면, 이 노래의 가사를 이해할 수 있어요.",
      "musicPlaying": true
    },
